ause you just wanted to see what it  was like or you're comfortable with guns  you like guns both yeah so I was with a  friend of mine who was formerly in law  enforcement and I wanted to see what the  what all the hype was about and then see  where you know why are so people  protecting these so viciously and I  think it's foolish I think we really do  need to revisit a ban on assault weapons  because those those have one purpose and  it's to kill and people don't need is  easy of access to them that they have  Johar let the CDC estimates that one in  five children experience a mental  disorder the president has talked about  that in Florida talked about improving  funds for mental health how do you see  that I think any improvement in mental  health it's something that we have  needed to address for a long time but I  see that as a larger societal issue you  know to talk about that as part of a  school safety policy I think just  distracts from what we should be talking  about you know allowing spaces for  students to learn in school keeping  students safe you know there are we have  social workers so how about we increase  the resources you know I'm in a school  in urban public school where every time  there's a budget cut we start to cut  resources to address things just like  you just said you know and even to your  last point your from your and I know  what you're saying I mean teachers know  how to teach I mean that's why there  were other social workers who are  supposed to address the problems that  Nick Cruz had down and back yeah my  husband is a detective we have guns in  our home you know but our roles are very  different we go to work to do very  different things you know I don't want  to carry a gun I want to stand in front  of kids I want to make sure that we  create a space for them to learn all of  these other things that are added on as  part of the conversation really confuse  what we're really talking about and  blurs the line between the roles 